Audit backend-to-TUI boundaries whose semantics are more demanding than replacing a displayed value: transcript and tool streaming, active-run event envelopes and queues, conversation versus local-command output, permission and question prompts, plugin UI requests, subagent workspace/inspector updates, branch-summary operations and asynchronous image/Mermaid delivery. Trace app adapters, TUI reducers/controllers and backend authorities; include TuiSubmitContext, TuiActiveRunQueues, runtime_plugin_ui.*, runtime_prompts_internal.*, app/tui/subagent_workspace.* and narrow transported Snapshot/Frame/view types. Identify all current backend implementation types and capabilities crossing the frontend boundary.

For each protocol classify its pieces as coalescible observable state, ordered event history, action request, correlated decision, immutable service dependency or control outcome. Document ordering, identity/ownership, permission validation, generation checks, cancellation, acknowledgement, backpressure/bounds, overflow and resynchronization behavior. State which pieces become canonical UnlockedData plus frontend projections, and how non-coalescible information remains lossless when dirtiness notifications coalesce. Evaluate a bounded backend journal/canonical accumulation with frontend cursors where appropriate; do not assume a single latest-value slot can replace a stream or that a notification authorizes an action. Any neutral delivery exception must have an explicit contract and rationale, not preserve an old state snapshot under a new name.

Produce a protocol-boundary artifact and contents entry with source references, proposed migration ownership, removal targets and regression scenarios. Preserve path-free subagent data, invocation-bound plugin requests, request-authorized transcript events and backend-owned permission decisions. Backend-internal snapshots may remain internal, but direct transfer of those snapshots or inspector frames into TUI must be accounted for. Identify existing focused tests and terminal scenarios for delayed responses, stale generations, eviction, cancellation, simultaneous prompts, local-command isolation and stream ordering. No implementation is authorized by this investigation; unresolved architectural choices go to reconciliation before the corresponding migration slice starts.
